# What a Bad Blood is told on taking a body, instead of the honourable hunters' entry message

cmu-bad-blood-entry-1 = You are a [bold]Bad Blood[/bold]: a Yautja cast out by the clans. The honour code does not bind you. Everyone who is not of your clan is prey.
cmu-bad-blood-entry-2 = [bold]The Lodge.[/bold] Your Leader pitches it with Pitch Camp, on open ground away from the prey's landing zones. It holds the spit, the armory, the kennel and the Ascension Stone. Defend it: a clan with no Leader and no Lodge is finished.
cmu-bad-blood-entry-3 = [bold]Superiority Points.[/bold] Offer polished trophies at the Lodge, cook your kills on its spit and raise Clan Totems. The clan spends what it earns on reinforcement squads, hounds, Totems and the armory.
cmu-bad-blood-entry-4 = [bold]Hunger and thirst.[/bold] You can only eat prey cooked on the Lodge's spit, and you drink water only. Starve and you slow down, bleed and lose your cloak.
cmu-bad-blood-entry-5 = [bold]Succession.[/bold] When the Leader falls, the clan votes for a new one at the Ascension Stone, and the old Leader's bracer destroys itself.
